    "Scouting Notes": "Reliever\n Analytical pitcher with a good plan of attack, that he believes in.\n Knows his stuff well, wonder if at times it causes him not to trust the new pitches he's working on (over thinking).\n Walks are a lot higher than you'd expect. Think it's less about his pure command and more about him trying to be too fine.\n Fastball jumps on hitters despite average velo, has great spin rate properties.\n Changeup is his out pitch, and the one he will likely get a large portion of his K's with. Very high level pitch.\n Slider shows improvements in 2022, but not consistent and still below average.\n Curve might have been scrapped? Not used much, if at all.\n If slider can be a decent third offering, likely a 5 starter in most rotations. In Brewers rotation, likely a swing man.\n Think his best role will be out of the pen in a multi inning role where his two pitch mix might play up more and he might throw a bit harder.",
